 topic=("Termite treatment and tent fumigation in Tampa",
        "<p>Tampa has both termite types that matter most in Florida: subterranean termites that come from the soil and drywood termites that live entirely inside wood. Subterranean colonies are usually handled with liquid soil treatments or bait systems. Drywood infestations that have spread through a structure often call for tent fumigation, where the home is sealed under tarps and filled with a fumigant gas, then aerated before you return. Smaller, contained drywood infestations can sometimes be spot-treated. A licensed inspection decides which approach fits; see <a href=\"/services/termite-control/\">termite control options</a>.</p>"),
